WEBVTT

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:04.330
Sat Five, right leg drive system,
output down by 27%.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.090
Calibrating balance mechanism
to compensate.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.400
I think my Ulm Blast is blown too.
Check that for me.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.500
Roger.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:12.070
Retarding mechanism's secondary
circuits are still good.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.000
You should be able to make
it back to base.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.270
Actually, I'm worried about the
stresses on the actuators.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:17.830
Please have the transporter
deployed.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.510
Is there a way for a transporter
to make it out here?

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.580
We have it taken care of.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.140
Right, then expedite the retrieval
of Sat Five and Sat Six.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:31.480
Sat Four's physical condition
is reviving again!

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.460
Sat Five and Six, watch
out for Sat Four!

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.920
Up!

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.800
Lock!

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.190
Sat Five, retreat!

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.360
Sat Five, Sat Five!

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.460
I can't get through. No response
from Sat Five.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:18.670
What about Sat Six?

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:19.470
No response either.
What about Sat Six?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.160
No response either.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.270
Big brother...

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.140
Please hurry!

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.160
It's using the lifting winch
end like a blade!

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.140
Captain Kitazawa!

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.550
What is it? What is he doing?

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.960
What is Sat Four doing?

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:20.120
Don't worry. This is a helicopter
that's with the SSDF,

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.680
the branch Yushiro and I are with.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:25.590
Where might you be taking us,
Lieutenant?

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.650
To Gowa City, Ma'am.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:37.860
Jeez, an Asian vein even in
a rural city like this one.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.630
I heard they've been popping
up all over Japan.

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:45.750
We should just go in and clean out
the place with a little napalm.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.240
Quit it!

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:51.720
Granted, they are a threat
to the security of Japan.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:01.990
Yes, that's right. Yushiro
is on his way here.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:06.460
I hear the pilot that infiltrated the
compound and vault is with him.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.500
All right.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.040
In any case, we can't do
anything with the kugai

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:12.530
until we bring it back to the labs.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:15.060
I'll be back soon.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.680
Kazukiyo...

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:42.140
Our father is worried about you.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.430
Go home, Misuzu.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.480
Big brother!

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:50.080
Misuzu!
Big brother!

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:50.980
Misuzu!

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.640
Yushiro and I have things
we need to talk about.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:04.220
I'm sorry. Go on home ahead of us.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.710
But...

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.230
You need not worry, Misuzu.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.470
I kept my promise, right?

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:18.930
I understand. I'll trust you,
big brother.

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:34.880
Go home quickly and relieve
our father's anxiety.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:10.090
That's right. The pilots are not
in any immediate danger.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.650
When will the medical team arrive?

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:14.500
Roger that.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:17.260
Are you all right,
Captain Kitazawa?

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:20.270
I'm fine, thank you, Sir.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:24.170
But what was he doing back there?

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:33.610
Sat Four did not try to destroy
Sat Six completely.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.170
No, I don't understand.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:41.750
Maybe it's collecting heads?

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:47.590
Either way, at this rate he'll make
it out of the training grounds.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.650
What's the remaining maximum
operational time frame of Sat Four.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:53.970
This is an estimate, but a maximum
of twenty hours and twenty minutes.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:58.100
Sat Four might leave the training
grounds for civilian districts.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:03.270
So in the end, are we going to have
to destroy him with artillery fire?

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:07.950
I will issue the command the
moment it leaves the grounds.

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:11.110
But if we still can save
Major Taniguchi, then...

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:17.420
So in other words, we are going to
have rely on Captain Gowa again.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.530
I've been told about what
happened at Kinashi.

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:27.830
I hear you were able
to man the kugai.

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:32.540
You've matched all the expectations
I had for you.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:34.630
You are truly worthy to
be my brother.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:46.710
That didn't take long.
She's the one.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:53.420
A girl? This is the one?

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:59.860
Yushiro, there are too many things
that need to be explained.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.100
I'd like to have both of you
cooperate with us.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:08.340
Cooperate? You make it sound
as if we had a choice.

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:12.110
Well, if you realize that much, then
we should have no problems

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.850
working with each other.

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:17.280
Kiyotsugu, I'll leave this
woman in your care.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.420
All right.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:19.890
Kiyotsugu...

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:21.380
Don't worry.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:24.980
We are precious test subjects.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.950
I'm sure they will take
good care of me.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:29.430
Isn't that right?

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:29.960
That's right. So please
cooperate with us.
Isn't that right?

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:32.520
That's right. So please
cooperate with us.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:35.420
I see.

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:40.230
You two first met each other
in Belgistan, right?

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:46.480
That's all fine, but we have
other business next.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:47.650
Orders have been handed
down to you

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:52.090
as a member of SSDF Training
Corps Experimentation Company.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:56.520
A Type 17 Improved version unit
went amok during trails

00:10:56.520 --> 00:11:00.460
being held at the Yausubetsu
Training Grounds in Hokkaido.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:04.360
Your order is to capture
this unit. So it says.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:07.930
Improved version? What happened?

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:10.670
It seems some accident happened
following a special procedure

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:12.670
that was conducted upon the pilot.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.780
Special procedure?

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:16.680
They say that unless
you're willing to go,

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:19.650
they'll give up capturing and
neutralize him instead.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:24.940
What's your decision?

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:28.380
I'll go, but...

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.320
There's something that I want
to ask you before I leave.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:33.830
All right.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:37.660
Gowa Yushiro died eight years ago.

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:42.370
Who am I?

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.430
You are

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:50.930
a kai.

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:03.910
Seventeen hours until the end
of maximum operations limit.

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:08.380
Will the pilot's, Major Taniguchi's,
body make it that far?

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.910
The flight from Iruma has arrived.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:26.970
I see. Captain Gowa has arrived.

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:32.350
The TA that he will be operating
should be ready soon.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:36.980
Captain Gowa's exceptional piloting
displayed in the Belgistan campaign

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.620
is our only remaining hope now.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.030
Colonel Hirokawa,

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:47.130
I won't pursue the issue of what
experiments were conducted here.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:50.200
But I do request that you closely
scrutinize the fact

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.670
that lives are being threatened as
a consequence from all this.

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:57.180
Soldiers on the frontlines are only
willing to risk their lives

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:00.450
when they believe that their leaders
consider them human beings,

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:03.110
and not some pawns
on the war map.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.130
Sat Seven, pilot heart rate, 145.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.670
Blood pressure, 157.

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.360
Physical condition is green.

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:27.970
Lock down piloting preset
data file B-001.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:29.870
Ground conditions data
transfer complete.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:35.710
Reduce right leg damper pressure
1.5 and left leg dampers 2.0.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:51.360
The four pilots, including Sat
Four's Major Taniguchi,

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:55.540
were given an injection of a
compound that was expected

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.970
to dramatically improve
their piloting abilities.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:00.570
An injection?

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.440
The compound consisted of a
globulin synthesized

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:05.540
from substances extracted from TA's
artificial muscles, the Mile One.

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:09.740
Understood. I'll do it.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:14.790
Sat Four is dangerously close to the
training ground boundaries.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.050
You will be restricted in
the use of firearms.

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:19.890
Understood.

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.060
Yushiro!
Understood.

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:21.260
Yushiro!

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:23.320
Captain Gowa, don't push this one.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:26.170
If you feel the situation is
getting out of hand,

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:27.970
pull back without hesitation.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.040
Once Sat Four comes within a
kilometer of the boundary,

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:32.470
the SSDF will let loose
an artillery barrage.

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:37.080
Confirming operational goals.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:40.880
Capture Sat Four after
crippling its mobility.

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:44.080
Primary target, knee
joint posterior.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:45.590
Secondary target...

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:48.420
Yushiro, why did you accept
an order like this?

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:49.890
Captain Ataka!

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:51.320
I'm sorry, but hold it.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:54.730
You heard him, about what
they were doing here.

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:55.560
There's no reason we... No reason
you should clean up their mess.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:56.230
There's no reason we... No reason
you should clean up their mess.

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:58.860
There's no reason we... No reason
you should clean up their mess.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:02.870
I can't abandon the
pilot of Sat Four.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:05.240
Well, yes...

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:08.610
But why should you have
to risk yourself in this?

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:11.000
Because he's just like me.

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:17.240
I'll be at the hangar.

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:23.880
What did he mean?

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:26.950
Just like him...

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:41.170
Captain Gowa will deploy soon.

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:43.180
Yes, I understand.

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:47.770
Please give all the data to Yonetani
once everything ends.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:50.710
Yes, you too.

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:01.890
What a wonderful younger brother.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:06.290
At least he's more useful
than the real one was.

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:12.570
I have Sat Four in my sights.
Start the operation.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.440
Sat Seven, copy.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:41.720
The target's response rate has
increased 300% above normal.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:01.780
Sat Seven's response rate is
at 322% above normal!

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:08.330
Capacity Phase Transition
has started.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:09.460
Amazing!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:13.490
Their responses are sky-rocketing
in response to each other.

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:16.470
Mile One is rewriting the movement
control program

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:18.730
superceding the control
program's commands?

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:37.790
Why does Sat Seven's response
seem so sluggish?

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:43.290
Captain Gowa must be holding back
as Major Taniguchi is in Sat Four.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.670
Retarding mechanism stresses,
exceeding 320%.

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:53.570
Left arm actuators, primary and
secondary, both down.

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:56.740
But the pilot's physical condition
is still positive.

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:23.300
What about Captain Gowa?

00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:24.540
He's all right.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.670
Call off the operation.

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:27.330
Sat Seven, pull back!

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:40.120
Sat Four has just gone beyond
the last security line.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.380
Colonel Hirokawa!

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.080
This is the 101st SSDF Battalion.

00:18:47.090 --> 00:18:49.460
Roger, preparing to
fire on position.

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:55.500
Target is in area B point 12-355,
heading northwest.

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:57.070
Based on the target's
current speed,

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.500
we will only get one barrage
to suppress its movement.

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:05.680
Air pressure, 980 millibars. Wind,
6 mph northwest. Humidity, 48%.

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:07.310
We have no time. We will not be
able to fire for range first.

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:08.010
Heads up. Warhead, adjusted
shrapnel rounds.

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:10.120
Heads up. Warhead, adjusted
shrapnel rounds.
Prepare to fire a three round burst
based on these instructions.

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:13.020
Charge three. Set fuse to
detonate upon impact.
Prepare to fire a three round burst
based on these instructions.

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:14.520
Confirming final check
of alignment.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:16.490
Distribution of fire, set to 2.5 mils.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:25.700
Captain Gowa, the SSDF artillery
will start firing any moment now.

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:28.390
Pull back! You're eighty meters
from being in the safe zone.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:36.640
This is headquarters.

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:38.700
Commence firing thirty-five
seconds from now.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.970
Starting countdown!

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:43.910
30...

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:50.080
25...

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:54.830
Go!

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:56.760
20...

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:58.250
Captain Gowa!

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:02.690
15...

00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:09.180
10... 9... 8...

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:12.180
7... 6... 5...

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:13.410
Captain Gowa!
4... 3... 2...

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:15.180
Call off the barrage!
4... 3... 2...

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:15.250
Call off the barrage!
1... Zero!

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:17.110
It's too late! They won't
get it in time!
1... Zero!

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:35.220
Impact!

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:03.160
I have positive life signs!

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:16.510
Sat Seven and Sat Four, vital of
pilots are positive.

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:20.180
Captain Gowa's heart rate and blood
pressure returning to normal.

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:22.170
He's fine! He's okay.

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:37.530
A shaped explosion, he dug a
trench with the ulm blast.

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:39.120
Dug into the ground...

00:21:54.350 --> 00:21:57.750
Denied to reach the threshold...

00:21:58.650 --> 00:22:03.650
I've become but a stain upon
the sword of Shichishi.

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:11.090
I've become but a stain upon
the sword of Shichishi...

00:22:29.790 --> 00:22:34.610
Hark

00:22:35.770 --> 00:22:41.060
It's time I journey

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:51.730
Break apart my heart

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:58.260
For crimson sadness

00:22:58.590 --> 00:23:05.770
Pours out from it

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:09.690
I can only, oh

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:12.880
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:12.970 --> 00:23:18.490
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:33.710 --> 00:23:37.590
I can only, oh

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:40.740
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:40.810 --> 00:23:45.940
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:47.470 --> 00:23:53.920
I beg you, be by my side

00:24:01.610 --> 00:24:06.240
The seventeen year long illusion
of Yushiro Gowa fades away.

00:24:07.350 --> 00:24:10.210
I am kai. So they say.

00:24:11.380 --> 00:24:13.050
But what is a kai?

00:24:13.920 --> 00:24:15.890
What does it mean to be a kai?

00:24:16.790 --> 00:24:18.420
Set to disembark

00:24:18.420 --> 00:24:21.290
I look back once more before
this journey begins

00:24:21.290 --> 00:24:24.560
So I may call the one I leave
behind my dear father

00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:28.700
I disembark in search
of my own self.
